T032 design context: quest state is three RefCounted logic classes (SideQuest, MainQuest, QuestLog) so tests never need a tree, mirroring CityProgress/SleepyDex; content lives in .tres (SideQuestDefinition per signature quest, MainRoute holding the ordered cities) because the unlock rule is route data, not balance. MainQuest keeps its own per-city beat maps beside CityProgress because the log is the route-level save face while CityProgress stays the run-local completion gate; both receive the same beats in the same CityRun handlers. QuestMarkers resolves objective targets through CityMap (tower node, arena block center, quest site markers) and filters side quests by definition.city_id so a later city's quest never draws in an earlier run. east_road_taken.connect is now unconditional: the travel beat belongs to the road, only the scene change needs a destination. Offer gating, dialogs, and the three signature quest flows stay with T033/T035/T037; save consumption lands with T040.
